# Wave W17-AA (Route 220): long sand — open-sea sand flecks, sparse: a cooler paler sand scattered thin under deep open water, the held-breath footing of the long empty sea (design: the long sea — north the Shingle road, east the Pal coast; spec-presence thin by nature, the R40 precedent, recorded in the plan). Route 220’s own sand — split from its twin Route 219’s bright sand by density entire (sparse flecks vs gold shallows) and from Route 219 by temperature: open-sea cool vs beach warm.
